      ":question/id": "228688c7-968e-5479-8983-65860e9b3e28",
      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{21}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{21}=3+(-1)\\cdot (3)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S &=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
